sdl2: show a held window with its first frame

Applies on top of 0029.

While Omarchy boots, the launcher hides a held window with an empty window
region, and nothing QEMU presents reaches a window with an empty region.
When the curtain lifted, the window showed what its surface held from before
the region went empty until QEMU's next frame: black, and on some GPUs a
white block where the window was first created. SDL paints a window black
only on the first erase in the process, which a held window misses while its
region is empty.

A held window is now also cloaked. DWM goes on composing a cloaked window,
so frames reach it, but nothing of it shows. Once the window is shown with a
region that is not empty, QEMU paints it black, draws a frame, and uncloaks
it once DWM's composed frame count has moved on since it presented a frame
at the size the window has then, in the same round when it can. QEMU only
reads the count and never waits on DWM, which can take far longer than a
frame with the display off or the session disconnected. If DWM cannot give
the count the window is uncloaked on the round after its frame. A window
resized, moved or given its frame back after its frame waits for one drawn
after that. It is uncloaked anyway a second after
it came on screen without such a frame, ten minutes after it was cloaked,
on Ctrl+Alt+F and when it is destroyed. If DWM refuses the cloak the window behaves as before, and a
refused uncloak is tried again on the next round.

